{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790424877,"nonce":"BTytBmQ+rl92Ad2LFxDNjnrZza4=","message":"Stage 3 inventory (llvm_backend at 12b72bb).\n\nHost addresses the lowering bakes in, each needing a symbol or an off switch in AOT mode:\n- call_helper / error_poll: helpers are called through resolve(name) as integer addresses with an all-i64 FunctionType. AOT: declare each by name, with its real signature.\n- ERROR_PENDING (error_poll) and JIT_DIRECT_DEPTH (direct_depth): statics read by address. AOT: export them as no_mangle data symbols from the runtime object and reference them as external globals.\n- jit_cur_cell / record_cell / site_mark / plant_record (frame records, stackmaps): JIT stack walking. Off in AOT.\n- safepoint_poll (jit_safepoint_page): off on wasm; stage 2 note stands.\n- field-kinds globals (add_global_mapping to class data), callsite IC pointers, jit_code_base, inline_bodies, cha: already Option / JIT-only. AOT passes None.\n- MCJIT engine creation, host_target_machine, stamp_function's host CPU attrs: AOT needs a TargetMachine from the triple and write_to_file(Object).\n\nHelper signatures on wasm32: 125 of the 137 RUNTIME_FN_NAMES are (u64...) -\u003e u64. The exceptions: pointer params in wren_call_dynamic, wren_make_closure_n, wren_osr_post, wren_osr_take; no return in wren_jit_roots_restore, wren_list_add, wren_map_set, wren_enter_shadow_frame, wren_exit_shadow_frame, wren_jit_frame_push, wren_jit_frame_pop, wren_ic_leave. The JIT's all-i64 declaration is harmless on 64-bit hosts but a signature mismatch on wasm (wasm-ld substitutes a trapping stub). Plan: a signature table beside RUNTIME_FN_NAMES, checked at compile time by coercing each helper to its declared extern \"C\" fn type, and read by the AOT declaration.\n\nCode sharing: aot.rs's front half (walk_imports, per-module MIR, classes, closures, CHA) holds cranelift DataId/FuncId inside AotModule. Split it so the LLVM path consumes the same module description and only the emitters differ (cranelift ObjectModule vs an LLVM Module), rather than a second walker.\n\nFirst vertical slice: one-module program without classes → LLVM AOT object for wasm32-wasip1 → bootstrap main → link with rust-lld against wlift_runtime.o (the stage 4 linker's differential reference) → run under wasmtime.","files":null}]}